	You need to compile everything with a "-debug" flag.  This
tells the compiler to set up information for the debugger.

	Edit the makefile.  Search for "cflags", which sets up the
compiler flags.  The first occurrence is the compiler flags for the
blind-player version.  Skip down a dozen lines, to right after the
"else".  

	Uncomment the two lines below where it says "Debugging".
Comment out the two lines below where it says "normal".  

	(This changes two compile time options.  It removes "-O",
optimization, which is very unhelpful when you're trying to debug.  
It adds "-pg", which just adds profiling information, which you
have no interest in.  It does not add debug info.)

	On the "cflags" line which you uncommented, add "-ggdb" 
right after "-pg".  (This gives you debug info usable by gdb.)  I'm
guessing that it has to go on the LFLAGS line, too, but I don't know.
Put it on and see if you get dozens of link-time error messages about
an unknown flag.

